          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A medicine in the bloodstream loses 20% of its amount every hour under a continuous exponential decay model. ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If 100 mg is injected at the start, after how long will less than 30 mg remain?",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer to the nearest minute.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "5 hours 24 minutes",
      "worked": "Let $h\\geq0$ be the elapsed time in hours.\n$$\\begin{align*}100(0.8)^h &< 30\\\\(0.8)^h &< 0.3\\\\h &> \\log_{0.8}(0.3)\\end{align*}$$\nTaking logarithms to base $0.8$ reverses the inequality because $0<0.8<1$. The threshold in minutes is\n$$60\\log_{0.8}(0.3)\\approx323.7305.$$\nTo the nearest minute, this is 324 minutes, or 5 hours 24 minutes.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
